1
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:08,133
HELLO.

2
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,760
WHAT'S THIS?

3
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:12,429
OH, RIGHT, IT'S THAT GIRL'S
PHONE NUMBER.

4
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:15,766
( sighs )

5
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:17,309
YEAH, YEAH, THERE IT IS.

6
00:00:17,309 --> 00:00:21,438
JUST A PHONE NUMBER
A REALLY HOT GIRL GAVE ME.

7
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:23,106
( chuckling )

8
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,692
IT'S NO BIG DEAL.

9
00:00:24,692 --> 00:00:27,862
I MEAN, IT IS HER HOME
PHONE NUMBER, BUT...

10
00:00:32,366 --> 00:00:33,325
WHOA!

11
00:00:35,327 --> 00:00:36,662
WH-WHOOPS.

12
00:00:36,662 --> 00:00:37,830
( chuckling )

13
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:39,957
ALMOST LOST THIS BABY.

14
00:00:39,957 --> 00:00:43,002
YEAH, THE LOVELY AMANDA
GIVES ME HER NUMBER

15
00:00:43,002 --> 00:00:45,044
AND I, I GO AND DROP IT.

16
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:46,755
( chuckles )

17
00:00:48,716 --> 00:00:49,842
( sneezes )

18
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:54,763
THANK YOU.

19
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:06,400
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

20
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,903
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

21
00:01:08,903 --> 00:01:11,279
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

22
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:16,243
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

23
00:01:16,243 --> 00:01:17,870
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

24
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:21,498
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

25
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:25,293
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

26
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:26,461
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

27
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:30,382
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

28
00:01:30,382 --> 00:01:31,592
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

29
00:01:31,592 --> 00:01:34,929
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

30
00:01:34,929 --> 00:01:39,892
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

31
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:45,981
RACHEL?
YEAH.

32
00:01:45,981 --> 00:01:47,024
WHEN'S YOUR BIRTHDAY?

33
00:01:47,024 --> 00:01:48,984
MAY 5. WHY?

34
00:01:48,984 --> 00:01:51,486
I'M JUST MAKING A LIST
OF PEOPLE'S BIRTHDAYS.

35
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:52,821
OH, MINE'S DECEMBER...

36
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:53,781
YEAH, WHATEVER.

37
00:01:58,326 --> 00:01:59,995
Chandler:
OH, SHE'S PRETTY.

38
00:01:59,995 --> 00:02:01,872
PRETTY, UH, PRETTY GIRL.

39
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:04,207
THE PRETTY...
SHE'S PRETTY.

40
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:06,668
WELL, JUST GO UP TO
HER AND ASK HER OUT.

41
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:09,004
WHAT'S THE WORST THING
THAT COULD HAPPEN?

42
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:11,172
I COULD DIE.

43
00:02:11,172 --> 00:02:13,717
YEAH, IT'S...
IT'S TOUGH BEING SINGLE.

44
00:02:13,717 --> 00:02:16,470
THAT'S WHY I'M SO GLAD
I FOUND AMANDA.

45
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:20,515
ROSS, YOU GUYS WENT OUT ONCE.

46
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,726
YOU TOOK YOUR KIDS
TO CHUCK E CHEESE

47
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:24,603
AND YOU DIDN'T EVEN KISS HER.

48
00:02:29,066 --> 00:02:31,485
I TELL PEOPLE SECRETS.

49
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:33,112
IT MAKES THEM LIKE ME.

50
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:36,865
OH.

51
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:38,909
HEY.
( sneezes )

52
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:42,037
OH, PHOEBE, YOU'RE SICK.
YOU SHOULDN'T PLAY.

53
00:02:42,037 --> 00:02:43,914
YOU SHOULD JUST GO HOME
AND GET IN BED AND STAY THERE.

54
00:02:43,914 --> 00:02:45,958
BUT I'M UNEMPLOYED.

55
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:48,710
MY MUSIC IS ALL I
REALLY HAVE NOW.

56
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:51,046
WELL, MUSIC AND
MAKING MY OWN SHOES.

57
00:02:51,046 --> 00:02:52,131
PRETTY, HUH?

58
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:55,634
( sneezes )

59
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:59,346
ALL RIGHT.
I'M GOING TO DO IT.

60
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:02,057
I'M GOING TO GO
GET SHOT DOWN.

61
00:03:02,057 --> 00:03:03,224
A-ANY ADVICE?

62
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:04,893
JUST BE YOURSELF.

63
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,520
BUT NOT TOO MUCH.

64
00:03:09,148 --> 00:03:10,398
WISH ME LUCK.

65
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:11,733
( loudly ):
GOOD LUCK.

66
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:16,488
WISH IT.

67
00:03:18,197 --> 00:03:21,743
HI. HI, I-I WAS JUST, UH,
SITTING OVER THERE AND...

68
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,954
UH, CHANDLER.
MY NAME'S CHANDLER.

69
00:03:23,954 --> 00:03:25,330
DID I SAY THAT?

70
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,331
NO, YOU DIDN'T.

71
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:27,708
HI, I'M KATHY.

72
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:29,208
KATHY WITH
A "K" OR A "C"?

73
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,919
WITH A "K."
H-H-HEY!

74
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:35,757
WOW. YOU ARE
REALLY GOOD AT THIS.

75
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:37,551
HEY, COME ON,
GIVE ME A BREAK.

76
00:03:37,551 --> 00:03:39,053
I'M OUT ON A LIMB HERE.
I'M SORRY. YOU'RE RIGHT.

77
00:03:39,053 --> 00:03:40,929
I APOLOGIZE,
BUT I SHOULD TELL YOU

78
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,139
THAT I'M WAITING
FOR A DATE.

79
00:03:42,139 --> 00:03:45,350
OH, AND THERE HE IS NOW.

80
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:46,434
HEY!

81
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:49,228
HEY! HEY-HEY, HEY.

82
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:51,899
I SEE YOU GUYS
ALREADY MET, HUH?

83
00:03:51,899 --> 00:03:54,068
YES, YES. I WAS JUST
TRYING TO FIGURE OUT A WAY

84
00:03:54,068 --> 00:03:56,820
TO DEMONSTRATE HOW I CAN GET
MY EXCEPTIONALLY LARGE FEET

85
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:00,074
INTO MY EVEN BIGGER MOUTH.

86
00:04:00,074 --> 00:04:02,242
DIDN'T I TELL YOU?

87
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:03,827
ALWAYS SHOWING OFF.

88
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:05,913
( chuckles )

89
00:04:05,913 --> 00:04:09,332
I... BEFORE I START I JUST
WANT TO SAY THAT I HAVE A COLD.

90
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:12,002
SO IF I SNEEZE
IN THE MIDDLE OF A SONG

91
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:13,670
IT'S NOT ON PURPOSE.

92
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:17,091
OH, EXCEPT THE LAST VERSE
OF "PEPPER PEOPLE."

93
00:04:17,091 --> 00:04:19,593
OKAY?

94
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:21,011
( clears throat )

95
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:22,971
( rasping ):
♪ SMELLY CAT ♪

96
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:24,514
♪ SMELLY CAT ♪

97
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:28,227
♪ WHAT ARE
THEY FEEDING YOU...? ♪

98
00:04:28,227 --> 00:04:32,231
THIS CHICK SOUNDS GOOD.

99
00:04:32,231 --> 00:04:34,233
♪ SMELLY CAT,
SMELLY... ♪

100
00:04:34,233 --> 00:04:36,235
HEY, GUNTHER,
BE A GOOD LITTLE BOY

101
00:04:36,235 --> 00:04:37,277
AND BRING ME
A WHISKEY.

102
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:47,662
HI.
HI.

103
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:49,206
GEEZ, AT 2:30
IN THE MORNING

104
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:51,291
I DIDN'T EXPECT TO HAVE
TO FIGHT OVER THE REMOTE.

105
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:53,961
SORRY. THERE'S THIS
ERNIE KOVACS THING

106
00:04:53,961 --> 00:04:55,378
ON IN A FEW MINUTES
I WANTED TO WATCH.

107
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,214
MY GOD, THAT'S WHY
I GOT UP, TOO.

108
00:04:57,214 --> 00:04:59,216
YOU'RE KIDDING?
OH, I LOVE HIM.

109
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:03,470
HEY, LISTEN, I'M SORRY
ABOUT THIS AFTERNOON.

110
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:05,513
YOU KNOW, IF I HAD
KNOWN YOU GUYS WERE...
I NEVER WOULD'VE...

111
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:07,057
( chuckling ):
OH, PLEASE!

112
00:05:08,642 --> 00:05:11,478
SO, JOEY TELLS ME
YOU TWO MET IN ACTING CLASS.

113
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:13,396
YEAH, THEY TEAMED US UP
AS PARTNERS

114
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:15,732
AND JOEY PICKED THREE SCENES
FOR US TO DO.

115
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,484
ALL OF THEM HAD US MAKING OUT.

116
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:20,195
THAT'S A GOOD THING,
ACTUALLY

117
00:05:20,195 --> 00:05:22,614
BECAUSE, UH, HE USED
TO MAKE ME REHEARSE WITH HIM.

118
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:25,492
OH-OH-OH-OH-OH!

119
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:26,868
OH, IS IT ON?

120
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:28,745
NO, BUT THIS WONDER
BROOM IS AMAZING!

121
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:29,704
HEY, WAIT.

122
00:05:31,248 --> 00:05:32,249
( gasps )

123
00:05:32,249 --> 00:05:33,208
OH, MY GOD!

124
00:05:35,169 --> 00:05:36,670
OH, IT'S ON, IT'S ON.

125
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:38,797
( music-box song playing )

126
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:45,428
HERE WE GO,
LITTLE FELLA.

127
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:47,097
( giggles )

128
00:05:47,097 --> 00:05:48,431
WHAT ABOUT THE DUCK?

129
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:49,891
WELL, THE DUCK CAN SWIM.

130
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,559
OF COURSE.

131
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:56,481
( throaty voice ):
♪ MY STICKY SHOE ♪

132
00:05:56,481 --> 00:06:00,359
♪ MY STICKY, STICKY SHOE ♪

133
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:03,071
♪ WHY YOU STICK ON ME ♪

134
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,573
♪ BABY? ♪

135
00:06:07,201 --> 00:06:08,952
THANKS FOR THE LIGHTS, HONEY.

136
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:14,124
Ross:
WAY TO GO.

137
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:16,668
YOUR COLD MAKES YOU
SOUND SO GREAT.

138
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:19,671
IT'S FUN.
GOD, I LOVE HOW SEXY I AM.

139
00:06:19,671 --> 00:06:21,756
( coughing )

140
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,260
KATH, WE SHOULD
GET GOING.

141
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:26,970
WE'RE GOING TO BUY HAMSTERS.

142
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:28,138
OH...

143
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:29,514
I LOVE THOSE LITTLE GUYS.

144
00:06:29,514 --> 00:06:31,058
NO, NO, IT'S
NOT LIKE THAT.

145
00:06:31,058 --> 00:06:33,977
I... I WORK FOR A
MEDICAL RESEARCHER.

146
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:36,479
WELL, HAVE FUN.

147
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,273
OKAY.

148
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:40,984
WELL, I THINK IT'S NICE
THAT THE MEDICAL COMMUNITY

149
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:43,195
IS FINALLY TRYING
TO HELP SICK HAMSTERS.

150
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:47,824
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I LIKE KATHY.

151
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,368
YEAH?
OH, YEAH, ME, TOO.

152
00:06:49,368 --> 00:06:51,328
SHE'S SO COOL AND PRETTY.

153
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:52,537
Phoebe:
YEAH, SHE'S...

154
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,581
SHE'S SMART AND...
FUNNY, YOU KNOW?

155
00:06:54,581 --> 00:06:57,084
I MEAN, WE WERE UP
ALL LAST NIGHT TALKING.

156
00:06:57,084 --> 00:06:58,668
SHE SAID
THE FUNNIEST THING

157
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:00,461
ABOUT-- WHAT?

158
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:04,174
YOU LOVE HER.

159
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:06,301
NO, I DON'T.

160
00:07:06,301 --> 00:07:10,347
YES, YOU DO.
CHANDLER LOVES KATHY.

161
00:07:10,347 --> 00:07:13,225
COME ON, PHEEBS,
NOW, JUST-- JUST LAY OFF HIM.

162
00:07:13,225 --> 00:07:14,559
THANK YOU, ROSS.

163
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:16,686
YEAH, HE'S A LITTLE
SENSITIVE RIGHT NOW

164
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:18,188
BECAUSE HE'S SO IN LOVE.

165
00:07:18,188 --> 00:07:19,314
ALL RIGHT.

166
00:07:19,314 --> 00:07:21,275
( all making kissing noises )

167
00:07:21,275 --> 00:07:23,693
OH, MM!
OH, KATHY!

168
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:25,445
KATHY,
I LOVE YOU.

169
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:26,696
OH!

170
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:28,031
( making kissing noises )

171
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:37,291
Phoebe:
SO, I NEED TO WRITE

172
00:07:37,291 --> 00:07:40,085
SOME DEPRESSING STUFF TO GO
WITH MY NEW BLUESY VOICE

173
00:07:40,085 --> 00:07:41,169
BUT NOTHING THAT SAD

174
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:42,712
HAS EVER REALLY HAPPENED TO ME.

175
00:07:42,712 --> 00:07:45,048
WELL, HOW ABOUT YOUR MOM DYING

176
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:47,968
OR HAVING TO LIVE ON THE STREETS
WHEN YOU WERE 14?

177
00:07:47,968 --> 00:07:50,971
UH-HUH.

178
00:07:50,971 --> 00:07:52,306
OH, YEAH,
I COULD WRITE ABOUT THE TIME

179
00:07:52,306 --> 00:07:54,557
MY HAIR DID
THAT WHOO-HOO THING.

180
00:07:57,311 --> 00:07:58,312
HEY.

181
00:07:58,312 --> 00:07:59,771
( both ):
HEY.

182
00:07:59,771 --> 00:08:02,274
SO, I'M GOING
OVER TO AMANDA'S TONIGHT...

183
00:08:02,274 --> 00:08:03,275
RACHEL'S NOT HERE.

184
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:05,193
OH.

185
00:08:07,279 --> 00:08:08,738
HOW'S IT GOING WITH HER?

186
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,365
GREAT, ACTUALLY.

187
00:08:10,365 --> 00:08:12,867
I'M THINKING TONIGHT
MAY BE THE NIGHT.

188
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:15,162
YEAH, THE KIDS ARE GOING
TO PLAY TOGETHER

189
00:08:15,162 --> 00:08:16,830
AND THEN,
WHEN THEY'RE ASLEEP

190
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:20,041
I'M THINKING AMANDA AND I
BREAK OPEN A BOTTLE OF WINE--

191
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:23,253
DO A LITTLE PLAYING
OURSELVES.

192
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:27,257
HI, GUYS.

193
00:08:27,257 --> 00:08:28,425
THIS IS JOSH.

194
00:08:28,425 --> 00:08:30,218
JOSH, THESE
ARE MY FRIENDS.

195
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,219
AND THAT'S ROSS.

196
00:08:32,262 --> 00:08:33,805
HI, JOSH.

197
00:08:33,805 --> 00:08:35,056
HI.

198
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:36,891
DUDES.

199
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:38,310
DID YOU PLAY IN COLLEGE?

200
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:39,769
OH, I STILL DO.

201
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:42,189
NEXT YEAR I HOPE
TO MAKE VARSITY, THOUGH.

202
00:08:42,189 --> 00:08:44,065
ROSS, DIDN'T YOU
PLAY SOCCER

203
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,150
IN HIGH SCHOOL?

204
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:47,152
OH, NO, WAIT,
THAT'S RIGHT.

205
00:08:47,152 --> 00:08:51,865
YOU JUST ORGANIZED
THEIR GAME SCHEDULES
ON YOUR COMMODORE 64.

206
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:53,200
WELL, IT'S GETTING LATE.
I GOT TO GET TO THE GAME,

207
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,575
SO I'M GOING TO HEAD.

208
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:55,535
OKAY.

209
00:09:00,457 --> 00:09:02,167
I'LL MISS YOU.

210
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:04,585
DOPE!

211
00:09:09,174 --> 00:09:10,884
WOW. CUTE ONE.

212
00:09:10,884 --> 00:09:12,260
VERY CUTE.

213
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,803
I KNOW. ISN'T HE GREAT?

214
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:15,472
IT'S SO NICE
TO FINALLY BE

215
00:09:15,472 --> 00:09:18,058
IN A FUN RELATIONSHIP,
YOU KNOW?

216
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:20,477
NOTHING BORING ABOUT HIM,
AND, UH...

217
00:09:20,477 --> 00:09:22,937
BET HE'S NEVER EVEN
SET FOOT IN A MUSEUM.

218
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,981
WELL, MAYBE HE'LL GET
TO GO SOON--

219
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:27,608
YOU KNOW, LIKE
ON A CLASS TRIP OR SOMETHING.

220
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:32,072
YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE IS
REALLY GREAT ABOUT HIM?

221
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:34,199
OH, WHAT IS THE
WORD FOR AN ADULT

222
00:09:34,199 --> 00:09:37,327
WHO DOESN'T HAVE
DINOSAUR TOYS IN
THEIR BEDROOM?

223
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:38,495
OH...

224
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:44,501
WHAT WAS THAT?

225
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:46,002
MONICA KNOWS.

226
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:48,338
IT'S THIS DUMB THING
THAT ROSS MADE UP

227
00:09:48,338 --> 00:09:50,090
TO TRY TO FOOL OUR PARENTS.

228
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:53,260
IT'S A WAY OF GIVING THE FINGER
WITHOUT ACTUALLY HAVING

229
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,678
TO GIVE IT.

230
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:58,432
I REMEMBER I CRIED
THE NIGHT YOU MADE THAT UP.

231
00:09:58,432 --> 00:10:01,184
IT WAS THE FIRST TIME
I REALIZED I WAS COOLER

232
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:03,186
THAN MY BIG BROTHER.

233
00:10:03,186 --> 00:10:04,312
WELL.

234
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:06,606
I'M GOING TO GO GET READY...

235
00:10:10,902 --> 00:10:13,988
FOR MY DATE TONIGHT, SO, UH...

236
00:10:13,988 --> 00:10:15,990
I'LL JUST HEAD.

237
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:22,163
YEAH, I SHOULD GO, TOO,
'CAUSE I'M PLAYING IN ONE HOUR.

238
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:23,790
( clears throat )

239
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:26,709
( normal voice ):
YOU GUYS SHOULD COME HEAR ME.

240
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:29,129
OOH! HEAR ME-- OOH!

241
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:30,589
♪ MY STICKY SHOES... ♪

242
00:10:30,589 --> 00:10:32,507
EWW! EWW! OH!

243
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:37,262
I LOST MY SEXY PHLEGM.

244
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:44,060
HI.
HI.

245
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,061
HI, BEN.

246
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:46,646
WOW, YOU-- YOU LOOK GREAT.

247
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:47,688
THANKS.

248
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:49,566
OKAY. HEY, TOMMY.

249
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:50,984
I AM SO GLAD

250
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:53,403
THAT YOU COULD
COME OVER TONIGHT.

251
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:54,404
OH, NO, NO.

252
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:57,449
IT'S MY PLEASURE.

253
00:10:57,449 --> 00:10:59,993
MY CELL PHONE NUMBER
IS RIGHT HERE ON THE COUNTER.

254
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:01,536
PLEASE HELP YOURSELF TO
ANYTHING IN THE FRIDGE.

255
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:02,621
WHA--

256
00:11:02,621 --> 00:11:03,997
I APPRECIATE THIS SO MUCH.

257
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:05,248
I HAVE BEEN TRYING TO
GO OUT WITH THIS GUY

258
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:07,750
FOR, LIKE, A MONTH.

259
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,127
I-I DON'T...

260
00:11:09,127 --> 00:11:10,670
OH, I DON'T MEAN
TO BE A SQUARE

261
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,046
BUT I'D REALLY APPRECIATE IT
IF YOU'D WAIT

262
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:16,259
AND DRINK YOUR WINE
AFTER THE KIDS ARE ASLEEP.

263
00:11:16,259 --> 00:11:19,095
GOODNIGHT, SWEETIE.

264
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:21,389
OH, THANKS FOR THIS.

265
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,724
I HOPE I CAN DO THE
SAME FOR YOU SOMETIME.

266
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:30,357
( sighs )

267
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:32,651
WHO WANTS TO MAKE
SOME LONG-DISTANCE CALLS?

268
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:43,911
KATHY!

269
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:45,997
KATHY! HI!

270
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:48,082
KATHY! KATHY!

271
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:58,134
KATHY!

272
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:04,891
FETCH! FETCH IT!

273
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:09,145
KATHY!

274
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:10,522
KATHY!

275
00:12:10,522 --> 00:12:11,481
KATHY!

276
00:12:12,649 --> 00:12:14,568
KATHY!

277
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:17,945
KATHY!

278
00:12:21,408 --> 00:12:23,410
( breathlessly ):
KA... KATHY.

279
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:26,663
HEY. CHANDLER,
WHAT'RE YOU DOING HERE?

280
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:27,664
WELL...

281
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:31,000
I JUST WANTED TO SAY, "HEY."

282
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,253
HEY.

283
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:35,171
OKAY.

284
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,464
( whimpers )

285
00:12:41,386 --> 00:12:44,264
YOU'RE MAKING IT SOUND
WORSE THAN IT WAS.

286
00:12:44,264 --> 00:12:46,641
HER DATE TIPPED ME TEN DOLLARS.

287
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:52,813
PHEEBS, WHAT
ARE YOU DOING?

288
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,566
OKAY, I WANT
TO BE SEXY AGAIN

289
00:12:54,566 --> 00:12:56,526
SO, I'M TRYING
TO CATCH A COLD.

290
00:12:56,526 --> 00:12:58,777
SHOULD BE EASY. SUPPOSEDLY,
THEY'RE PRETTY COMMON.

291
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:01,281
PHOEBE,
YOU'LL CATCH PNEUMONIA.

292
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:05,952
OKAY, YOU WERE RIGHT.

293
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:07,828
I'M IN LOVE
WITH JOEY'S GIRLFRIEND.

294
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:09,289
WHAT?
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

295
00:13:09,289 --> 00:13:11,999
HOW IS THAT POSSIBLE?
YOU BARELY KNOW HER.

296
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:14,419
I DON'T KNOW.
I CAN'T... I JU...

297
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:16,879
I CAN'T GET HER OUT OF MY HEAD,
YOU KNOW?

298
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:18,005
I MEAN, I'M A VERY BAD PERSON.

299
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:19,840
I'M A VERY, VERY BAD PER...

300
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,968
I'M A HORRIBLE PERSON.

301
00:13:23,762 --> 00:13:25,012
NO, YOU'RE NOT, CHANDLER.

302
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:26,431
WE STILL LOVE YOU, CHANDLER.

303
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:30,518
( sneezes )

304
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:31,852
OH... GOSH, PHOEBE,

305
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,104
I THINK
I CAUGHT
YOUR COLD.

306
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:34,731
YOU MEAN YOU STOLE IT.

307
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:37,400
( sneezes )

308
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:40,528
DON'T COVER YOUR MOUTH
WHEN YOU DO THAT.

309
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:42,489
( both laughing )

310
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:43,698
OH...

311
00:13:43,698 --> 00:13:45,700
WE WERE JUST TALKING
ABOUT YOU.

312
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:48,161
REALLY.

313
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:50,580
YEAH, I TOLD HER ABOUT
THE TIME YOU GOT DRUNK

314
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,040
AND FELL ASLEEP WITH
YOUR HEAD IN THE TOILET.

315
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,875
( laughing )

316
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:56,503
RIGHT IN THERE.

317
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,883
...NINETY-NINE

318
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:04,218
A HUNDRED.

319
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:05,844
READY OR NOT, HERE I COME!

320
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:12,059
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO OVER
THE CONCEPT ONE MORE TIME.

321
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:13,227
HEY.

322
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:15,480
HEY.

323
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,064
LISTEN, YOU WANT
TO GET SOME DINNER

324
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:18,065
WITH ME AND KATHY
TONIGHT?

325
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:19,942
OH, UM, YOU KNOW WHAT?

326
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:21,611
I, UH, ALREADY ATE.

327
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:23,863
IT'S 4:30.

328
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:26,240
YEAH, WELL, I HAD A
BIG MEAL ON MONDAY.

329
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:28,242
SO THAT'S JUST
GOING TO GET ME

330
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,577
STRAIGHT THROUGH
THE WEEK.

331
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:31,245
OKAY.

332
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:32,955
I SEE WHAT'S GOING ON HERE.

333
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,501
YOU, YOU DO?

334
00:14:36,501 --> 00:14:38,169
YEAH. YOU DON'T LIKE KATHY.

335
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:41,214
YOU GOT ME.

336
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:42,674
YEAH. YOU BEEN
AVOIDING HER

337
00:14:42,674 --> 00:14:44,467
EVER SINCE
WE STARTED GOING OUT.

338
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:46,219
I MADE AN EFFORT
TO LIKE JANICE.

339
00:14:46,219 --> 00:14:49,096
IT'S YOUR TURN
TO MAKE AN EFFORT TO LIKE KATHY

340
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:51,057
BY COMING OUT TO DINNER WITH US.

341
00:14:51,057 --> 00:14:52,726
RIGHT?
YEAH, RIGHT.

342
00:14:52,726 --> 00:14:55,895
GOOD. AND, HEY, MY TREAT.

343
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,938
BUT THAT'S ONLY BECAUSE YOU'RE
NOT EATING ANYTHING, RIGHT?

344
00:14:57,938 --> 00:14:59,190
RIGHT.

345
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:05,697
ROSS ISN'T HERE.

346
00:15:05,697 --> 00:15:06,989
OH.

347
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:08,491
STOP IT!

348
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:13,663
SO, UH, I'LL SEE YOU
AT THE PARTY?

349
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:15,373
FEAR'S FEAR, MAN!

350
00:15:15,373 --> 00:15:17,166
TWENTY-FOUR/SEVEN!

351
00:15:18,209 --> 00:15:19,419
YEAH!

352
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:24,632
I AM SO GOING TO MARRY THAT GUY.

353
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:27,719
OH!

354
00:15:27,719 --> 00:15:28,969
WHAT?

355
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:30,680
I THINK HE'S STEALING FROM ME.

356
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:32,473
WHY?

357
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:34,475
BECAUSE HE'S STEALING FROM ME.

358
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:36,143
OH!

359
00:15:36,143 --> 00:15:37,978
HI. IT'S ME.

360
00:15:37,978 --> 00:15:39,146
AND SOUP.

361
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:40,523
HEY, OH, I JUST SAW JOSH.

362
00:15:40,523 --> 00:15:42,817
HE LOOKED SO YUMMY
IN YOUR LEATHER JACKET.

363
00:15:42,817 --> 00:15:44,903
UGH!

364
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:48,989
HERE. NOW,
I DON'T EAT CHICKEN

365
00:15:48,989 --> 00:15:50,658
SO, IT'S JUST NOODLE SOUP.

366
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:51,785
AND THERE'S

367
00:15:51,785 --> 00:15:52,993
NO CHICKEN
IN THE BROTH EITHER

368
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:55,622
SO, IT'S REALLY
JUST NOODLE WATER.

369
00:15:57,331 --> 00:15:58,999
THANK YOU SO MUCH,
PHOEBE.

370
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:01,753
SURE.

371
00:16:01,753 --> 00:16:03,463
WHAT ARE YOU DOING WITH THOSE?

372
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:05,673
I NEED YOUR GERMS.

373
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,133
I WANT MY COLD BACK.

374
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:10,177
I MISS MY SEXY VOICE.

375
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:11,846
SORRY, PHOEBE.

376
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:13,514
THAT'S OKAY.

377
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,683
HOW'S THE SOUP?

378
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:17,644
MMM.

379
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,688
OHH!

380
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:21,773
GOD!

381
00:16:21,773 --> 00:16:23,232
GROSS!

382
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,365
( laughing )

383
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:33,827
OH, MY GOD, YOU GUYS,
CHECK IT OUT.

384
00:16:33,827 --> 00:16:36,078
YOU CAN SEE
THAT GIRL'S UNDERWEAR.

385
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:37,538
IS SHE GREAT OR WHAT?

386
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,915
SO? HUH?

387
00:16:38,915 --> 00:16:41,501
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

388
00:16:41,501 --> 00:16:43,628
UH, SHE'S, SHE'S
NOT REALLY MY TYPE.

389
00:16:43,628 --> 00:16:44,712
NOT YOUR TYPE?

390
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:45,755
SHE'S GORGEOUS.

391
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:47,465
YOU KNOW WHAT
I THINK IT IS?

392
00:16:47,465 --> 00:16:50,468
I THINK IT'S THE FISHNET
STOCKINGS, YOU KNOW?

393
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:52,261
WHENEVER I SEE A GIRL
IN FISHNET STOCKINGS

394
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:54,096
IT REMINDS ME OF...

395
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,015
MY FATHER IN
FISHNET STOCKINGS.

396
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:58,601
OKAY.

397
00:16:58,601 --> 00:17:00,353
UNDERSTANDING
A LITTLE MORE OF
WHY YOU'RE SINGLE.

398
00:17:00,353 --> 00:17:02,229
YOU KNOW, I HAVE
A FRIEND YOU'D LIKE.

399
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:04,983
SHE'S REALLY PRETTY,
AND THEN WE COULD
DOUBLE DATE.

400
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:07,318
UH, NO, NO, THANKS.

401
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:09,487
OKAY. I'VE GOT
SOME UGLY FRIENDS

402
00:17:09,487 --> 00:17:11,614
AND THEY'RE
ALL AVAILABLE, TOO.

403
00:17:11,614 --> 00:17:14,367
LISTEN, I'M GOING
TO GRAB A BEER.

404
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:17,119
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK, OKAY?

405
00:17:23,041 --> 00:17:24,377
WHAT WAS THAT?

406
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:25,670
WHAT?

407
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:27,922
KATHY WAS BEING NICE,
AND YOU WALKED AWAY.

408
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:29,215
I THOUGHT WE HAD A DEAL.

409
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:31,300
LOOK, WHAT DO
YOU WANT FROM ME?

410
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:33,427
I WANT YOU TO LIKE HER

411
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:35,638
BUT IF THAT'S TOO DAMN
DIFFICULT FOR YOU

412
00:17:35,638 --> 00:17:37,264
THEN THE LEAST
YOU COULD DO IS PRETEND.

413
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:38,725
I AM PRETENDING.

414
00:17:38,725 --> 00:17:40,518
WELL, THEN DO IT BETTER.

415
00:17:40,518 --> 00:17:44,438
WHAT DO YOU SAY
I GO AND TELL HER
HOW MUCH I LIKE HER?

416
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:45,857
NO, NO. IT'LL BE GOOD.

417
00:17:45,857 --> 00:17:47,441
I CAN TELL HER I BEEN
THINKING ABOUT HER--

418
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:48,442
THAT I HAVEN'T STOPPED
THINKING ABOUT HER

419
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:50,069
SINCE THE MOMENT WE MET

420
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,946
THAT I'M SO
FANTASTICALLY
OVER-THE-TOP

421
00:17:51,946 --> 00:17:54,323
WANT-TO-SLIT-MY-OWN-
THROAT IN LOVE WITH HER

422
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:56,576
THAT FOR EVERY MINUTE OF
EVERY HOUR OF EVERY DAY

423
00:17:56,576 --> 00:18:00,120
I CAN'T BELIEVE
MY OWN BAD LUCK THAT
YOU MET HER FIRST!

424
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,373
YEAH, WELL,
THAT'S PRETTY GOOD.

425
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,712
BUT YOU MIGHT WANT
TO TONE IT DOWN A LITTLE.

426
00:18:13,091 --> 00:18:14,343
HEY.

427
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:17,096
SO, UH, AMANDA JUST,
JUST DROPPED ME OFF.

428
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:19,139
YOU KNOW, THAT'S ONE
OF THE THINGS

429
00:18:19,139 --> 00:18:20,725
I LOVE ABOUT HER.

430
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:22,894
SHE'S, UH,
SHE'S OLD ENOUGH TO DRIVE.

431
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:25,605
SO, UH, I GUESS

432
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:28,441
YOU'RE NOT GOING TO MOM
AND DAD'S TONIGHT, HUH?

433
00:18:28,441 --> 00:18:29,984
( coughing ):
NO, SORRY.

434
00:18:29,984 --> 00:18:31,444
WELL, WHERE'S AMANDA?

435
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:33,153
COULD YOU GET ME
SOME COUGH DROPS?

436
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:35,531
YOU KNOW, I'M THINKING
YOU COULD BRING HER

437
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:37,825
AND YOU GUYS COULD GO
UP TO YOUR OLD ROOM

438
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:39,159
AND NOT MAKE OUT.

439
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:40,202
( coughing )

440
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:42,038
ROSS, A COUGH
DROP, PLEASE?

441
00:18:42,038 --> 00:18:44,206
AT LEAST I KNOW
SHE'S NOT GOING OUT WITH ME

442
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:45,708
TO GET INTO "R"-RATED MOVIES.

443
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:47,501
( coughing )

444
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:49,420
WHY DON'T YOU
JUST MARRY HER?

445
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:50,880
OH, NO, WAIT A MINUTE.

446
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:52,465
YOU CAN'T. I'M SORRY.
I FORGOT.

447
00:18:52,465 --> 00:18:54,258
SHE'S NOT A LESBIAN.

448
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:58,387
SEE, AMANDA
AND I HAVE A...

449
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:00,431
YOU HAVE NOTHING!

450
00:19:00,431 --> 00:19:01,724
YOU'RE NOT EVEN GOING OUT.

451
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:04,060
YOU'RE HER BABY-SITTER.

452
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:06,479
YOU HAVE
A 12-YEAR-OLD GIRL'S JOB.

453
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:11,358
( laughing )

454
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:16,990
OH, THAT IS SO SAD.

455
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:18,699
( laughing )

456
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:20,200
AND WHAT ARE YOU LAUGHING AT

457
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:23,203
MISS "MY KEG-SUCKING BOYFRIEND
IS STEALING FROM ME"?

458
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:26,040
( stifled laugh )

459
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,250
SO HE STOLE A COUPLE BUCKS
FROM ME.

460
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,585
BIG DEAL.

461
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:31,545
HE BOUGHT ME SOMETHING
WITH IT.

462
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,630
THAT'S MINE!

463
00:19:36,050 --> 00:19:40,013
NOW, WOULD YOU BOTH
PLEASE START ACTING LIKE ADULTS?

464
00:19:40,013 --> 00:19:41,597
AND GET ME MY COUGH DROPS?

465
00:19:44,058 --> 00:19:45,184
FINE.

466
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:46,435
SORRY.

467
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:47,561
HERE.

468
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:49,605
THANK YOU.

469
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:51,149
( sighs )

470
00:19:51,149 --> 00:19:54,360
LEAST I MADE TEN BUCKS
IN MY RELATIONSHIP.

471
00:19:56,112 --> 00:19:57,404
YOU KNOW...

472
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:07,414
♪ PARADING GOATS ARE PARADING ♪

473
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,583
♪ PARADING DOWN THE STREET ♪

474
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:13,129
♪ PARADING GOATS ARE PARADING ♪

475
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:15,173
♪ LEAVING LITTLE TREATS. ♪

476
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:17,675
I DON'T KNOW.

477
00:20:17,675 --> 00:20:20,053
DOES IT EVEN WORK
WITHOUT MY SEXY VOICE?

478
00:20:20,053 --> 00:20:21,512
I LIKE IT.

479
00:20:21,512 --> 00:20:22,596
( sneezes )

480
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:23,848
GUNTHER, KISS ME.

481
00:20:23,848 --> 00:20:24,974
W-WHAT?

482
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:38,236
( Kathy giggling )

483
00:20:41,157 --> 00:20:43,617
( turns up volume )

484
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:45,285
HEY.

485
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:49,623
NOW, WE'RE NOT EXACTLY
GOING TO BE SLEEPING IN HERE

486
00:20:49,623 --> 00:20:51,876
BUT DO YOU MIND?

487
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:53,252
( door shuts )

488
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,676
CAN I SLEEP ON YOUR COUCH?

489
00:21:13,147 --> 00:21:18,111
♪ AND I'M STILL WAITING
FOR MY PAPIER-MáCHé MAN. ♪

490
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:23,241
THANK YOU, MY BABIES.

491
00:21:27,078 --> 00:21:28,162
RACHEL?

492
00:21:28,162 --> 00:21:29,789
YEAH.

493
00:21:29,789 --> 00:21:32,041
I DON'T KNOW IF YOU HEARD
